    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@value": "We Remember"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@value": "In collaboration with the Toronto Children’s Chorus - The Chamber Choir and T.C.C.’s Toronto Youth Choir, we present a special commemoration concert of the 100th anniversary of Armistice Day. We will perform works relating to war and peace that represent the four Allied Nations: Australia, Canada, New Zealand and the United Kingdom. The program will feature a new world première of WWI popular songs arranged by Canadian Composer Stuart Calvert.\r\nParticipants include:\r\n\r\n \tChoirs\r\n\r\n \tToronto Children’s Chorus, Elise Bradley, conductor\r\n \tElmer Iseler Singers, Lydia Adams, conductor\r\n\r\n\r\n \tMusician\r\n\r\n \tStan Klebanoff, trumpet\r\n\r\n\r\n \tGuest Conductor\r\n\r\n \tBob Chilcott (UK) who will conduct his Peace Mass as well as other contributions within the concert.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThis will be a very special moment in time to join with the youth of the Toronto Children’s Chorus as we “Remember”.\r\n\r\n[maxbutton name=\"Tickets\"]"
      }
    ]
