    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@value": "Montreal with SMAM"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@value": "[caption id=\"\" align=\"alignnone\" width=\"562\"] Five Centuries for 40 Voices[/caption]\r\n\r\nDelighted with its collaborations with the Choir of Trinity Wall Street (New York) in 2014 and with The Elora Singers in 2016, the SMAM is joining forces with Toronto’s excellent Elmer Iseler Singers this year to once again present a choral concert for 40 voices. The repertoire covers five centuries of choral music, from the work of great 15th century master Johannes Ockeghem to present day compositions, including certain monumental works by Guerrero, Marenzio, Lassus, Tomkins, and Gibbons, and a few contemporary masterpieces by Quebecer Claude Vivier and Canadian composers Murray Schafer, Hussein Janmohamed, Peter Togni, Imant Raminsh, and Healey Willan, Canada’s leading composer of choral works.\r\n\r\nTickets available from the SMAM website.\r\nProgram\r\nXVth, XVIth, XVIIth, XXth et XXIth century Choral Works\r\nPresenting\r\n40 singers of the SMAM and the Elmer Iseler Singers (Toronto)\r\nA cappella choirs\r\nLydia Adams Andrew McAnerney, codirection"
      }
    ]
  },
