      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@value": "A Wilderness of Sea"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@value": "Vancouver Chamber Choir, Kari Turunen, conductor\r\nElmer Iseler Singers, Lydia Adams, conductor\r\n\r\nTwo of Canada’s premier ensembles take the stage together – an event not to be missed! The broad theme is the sea and the Vancouver Chamber Choir will present two new works on that theme, with both choirs joining forces in a magical work that has all too long gone unnoted: Toivo Kuula’s Meren virsi (The Hymn of the Sea).\r\n\r\nTickets to individual concerts are available online at the TicketMaster website.\r\n\r\nStudent rush tickets are available at the door, one hour before the concert for just $15!\r\nRepertoire\r\nAlex Freeman • A Wilderness of Sea\r\nToivo Kuula • Meren virsi\r\nCharles van Hemelryck • Présence\r\nStephen Chatman • Due East\r\n\r\nPLUS:\r\nadditional repertoire performed by the Elmer Iseler Singers"
      }
    ]
  },
