        "@id": "https://www.elmeriselersingers.com/events/agincourt-collegiate-institute-concert/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@value": "Agincourt Collegiate Institute concert"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@value": "Note: Possible postponement because of pending strike.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nMembers of Agincourt Collegiate music program have been an integral part of the world premiere of Timothy Corlis' newest work, Om Saha Navavatu and the Elmer Iseler Singers are pleased to present the work with those students on November 9th at Agincourt CI.\r\n\r\nAdmission is free and is generously funded by the Canada Council for the Arts and The Ontario Arts Council. General seating. Donations accepted at the door for ACI Music Department.\r\n\r\nOm Saha Nāvavatu (may we all be protected and blessed) is a meditational sound journey, a 40-minute choral voyage. A soothing, calming soundscape, Om Saha Nāvavatu is an invitation to let go of anger, prejudice and negativity to embrace pluralism and peace, allowing the mind to meander and feel suspended in time. The introspective, transformative work is inspired by Vedic texts and the poetry of Hindu and Buddhist Spiritual Masters.\r\n“Om Saha Nāvavatu is really a call for peace and hope in the world,” comments composer Timothy Corlis.\r\n\r\n\r\nFor more information contact us at 416-416-217-0537 or info@elmeriselersingers.com"
      }
    ]
