      {
        "@value": "Triple Choir Splendour: Sonic Light &#8211; EIS Toronto Series Concert #3"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@value": "Featuring EIS with the VIVA Chamber Singers, Carol Ratzlaff conductor, as part of our ongoing association and educational mentorship and an introduction to our audience of the newly formed Chroma Vocal Ensemble, Mitchell Pady conductor. This concert includes the spectacular Mass for Double Choir by Frank Martin along with Prayer for Peace by Eleanor Daley and grandmother moon by Peter Togni.\r\nTickets for Triple Choir Splendour: Sonic Light\r\nProgram\r\nO Radiant Light by James MacMillan\r\nLux Aurumque by Eric Whitacre\r\nThe Spheres by Ola Gjeilo\r\nCarol Ratzlaff, conductor\r\nSun on Water by Hussein Janmohamed\r\nLydia Adams, conductor\r\nThe Sun Never Says by Dan Forrest\r\ngrandmother moon, 1 and 4 by Peter Togni\r\nConstellation by Marie-Claire Saindon; poem by Herménégilde Chiasson\r\nMitchell Pady, conductor\r\nMass for Double Choir by Frank Martin\r\nPrayer for Peace by Eleanor Daley\r\nLydia Adams, conductor\r\n\r\n\r\nThanks to our Sponsors\r\nWe also appreciate the generous contributions of hundreds of individual donors."
      }
    ]
  },
