    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@value": "Choral and Organ Tapestry"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@value": "[caption id=\"attachment_4510\" align=\"alignright\" width=\"194\"] click the image to open the PDF of the concert program[/caption]\r\n\r\nPart of Roy Thomson Hall’s 2024 ANNUAL FREE NOON HOUR CHOIR &amp; ORGAN CONCERTS series, The Elmer Iseler Singers are pleased to present Choral and Organ Tapestry with Shawn Grenke, organist.\r\n\r\nRoy Thomson Hall’s magnificent Gabriel Kney pipe organ is featured alongside the artistry of Canada’s finest choirs and organists. The community is invited to enjoy an hour of beautiful music in the splendour of this acoustically superb venue.\r\n\r\nAll concerts begin at 12 Noon; NO Intermission\r\nFront Doors open at 11am; Auditorium Doors open at 11:30am\r\n\r\nTo reserve your tickets click here or visit the Roy Thomson Hall event page here\r\n\r\nFor orders of 20 tickets or more, please call 416-872-4255.\r\nSchool groups and senior centres please email contactus@mh-rth.com for group reservations.\r\n\r\nRoy Thomson Hall offer this free concert series thanks to the tremendous support of the Edwards Charitable Foundation and their community of education and outreach donors.\r\n\r\nFor more information about the NOON HOUR CHOIR &amp; ORGAN CONCERTS series click here."
      }
    ]
  },
