    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@value": "A Portrait in Song: The Music of Eleanor Daley"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@value": "Lydia Adams, conductor; Shawn Grenke, piano/organ\r\n\r\nThe brilliant work of composer Eleanor Daley has been celebrated and sung by choirs across Canada and throughout the world. Tonight, we celebrate this most beloved and cherished of Canada’s composers through works written with the warmth and stunning beauty which is a hallmark of Eleanor Daley’s writing. Works performed will include Eleanor’s major masterpiece, Requiem and other masterworks ‘The Angels Will Guide You Home’; Paradise and Prayer for Peace, among many.\r\n\r\nProgram\r\n\r\n\r\nThanks to our Sponsors\r\nWe appreciate the generous contributions of hundreds of individual donors."
      }
    ]
  },
