  {
    "@id": "https://elmeriselersingers.com/temporary/1de9a2d2-0e86-4900-9bd3-f5a74e7f6496",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Event"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.elmeriselersingers.com/events/choral-connections/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/startDate": [
      {
        "@type": "http://schema.org/Date",
        "@value": "2025-10-26"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/endDate": [
      {
        "@type": "http://schema.org/Date",
        "@value": "2025-10-26"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/location": [
      {
        "@id": "_:g2564800"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.elmeriselersingers.com/events/choral-connections/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@value": "Choral Connections"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@value": "A Must Come event for Canadian composers, choirs and commissioners!\r\n\r\nHello EIS Friends! \r\n\r\nAre you a conductor or someone planning to commission a Canadian composer, and wondering how to start planning?\r\n\r\nAre you a composer just waiting for a call to write something for choir, and want to get started on a commission?\r\n\r\nWell - this afternoon is for YOU!\r\n\r\nJoin sponsors Choirs Ontario and the Canadian Music Centre Ontario for a ’speed dating’ afternoon putting together composers and potential commissioners into the same room to discuss how to get started in meeting composers and conductors, and commissioning a new Canadian work for your choir - perhaps to honour a special choir anniversary - or a dedicated long-serving volunteer in your community - or to honour someone who is no longer with us - or to celebrate a wedding or a new baby - there are countless events and reasons to commission a new work. Come out - meet some really keen choral writers and creators - and let’s get some new works written!\r\n\r\nThere will be food to sustain us and lots of great advice and chat, including a discussion with Matthew Emery and Lydia Adams on the joys of commissioning choral music!\r\n\r\nSpace is limited, so please RSVP ASAP to Choral Connections at https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/choral-connections-tickets-1373624280199"
      }
    ]
  },
