    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@value": "The Spirit of Nature!"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@value": "Celebrating the Festival of the Sound’s 40th Anniversary\r\n[caption id=\"attachment_773\" align=\"alignright\" width=\"300\"] Elmer Iseler Singers, Festival of The Sound, July 2018 (Photo: Mark Rash)[/caption]\r\n\r\nIn the first Toronto series concert, we will present the program set out at the opening concert of 40th anniversary of Parry Sound's Festival of the Sound (which also coincided with our 40th anniversary year).\r\n\r\nThe program will include the Toronto Premiere of “The Sound – A Musical Evocation of Georgian Bay” by Eric Robertson, text by Gary Michael Dault.\r\nThere will be a Prelude concert followed by refreshments at 2:00pm.\r\n\r\nSpecial guest artists:\r\n[caption id=\"attachment_1291\" align=\"alignright\" width=\"230\"] Renowned Canadian actor Colin Fox brought his signature clear and thoughtful speaking style to the narrated portions. The Elmer Iseler Singers drew out the many beauties in Robertson’s score...” Review by Ken Stephen, Parry Sound North Star[/caption]\r\n\r\n \tNarrator\r\n\r\n \tColin Fox\r\n\r\n\r\n \tMusicians\r\n\r\n \tPenderecki String Quartet\r\n \tJames Campbell, clarinet\r\n \tBob Mills, double bass\r\n \tSuzanne Shulman, flute\r\n \tBeverley Johnson, percussion\r\n \tGuy Few, piano\r\n \tShawn Grenke, organ\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n[maxbutton name=\"Tickets\"]\r\nConcert program:"
      }
